            <ArticleTitle>Cost effectiveness of magnetic resonance imaging of the knee.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>475-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When compared to diagnostic arthroscopy in patients with knee complaints consistent with internal derangement, MR imaging emerges as a cost effective diagnostic supplement to clinical examination. This article concludes that the results of MR imaging can be used as a guide for the management of knee pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
